dtlogin.msg: leave out the two help messages over the catalogue limit.

Set 3 messages 1 and 3 are the login screen's and the chooser's help
(1567 and 1448 bytes). A System V catalogue message holds at most 1024 bytes (NL_TEXTMAX), and
gencat refuses the whole file for one longer message. The C catalogue
leaves them out, with a comment; catgets then returns the program's
built-in text, which is the same text. A translated catalogue
cannot carry them while the limit stands.

--- a/programs/dtlogin/dtlogin.msg	2026-11-20 12:03:13
+++ b/programs/dtlogin/dtlogin.msg	2026-11-20 12:03:13
@@ -218,49 +218,7 @@
